# The list of work was one file, TODO.md, and every branch edited it at the head
# of the same two sections. A three-way merge calls that a conflict, so this
# file marked it `merge=union` to keep both sides instead of asking.
#
# That is gone, and the rule with it. The list is `todo/`, one file per item,
# so two branches touching different items have nothing in common to conflict
# over and there is nothing for a merge driver to resolve. See `todo/README.md`
# for why, including the two things union merge could not do: reach GitHub's
# mergeability check, which does not read this file, and express a deletion.
#
# Nothing here needs a custom driver. Leave it that way — a driver that git
# honours and GitHub ignores buys a clean local merge and a conflict banner on
# every pull request, which is worse than either on its own.
